+### Duration
+
+{class}`Duration` converts a string into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. Its metavar is `DURATION`.
+
+Accepted formats are a whole number of seconds (`120`), or `<integer><unit>` groups using the units
+`d`, `h`, `m` and `s`, each at most once, in that order, with no spaces and case-insensitive
+(`2d`, `1h30m`, `45S`, `1d2h3m4s`). Negative values, decimals and other units are rejected.
+
+```python
+@click.command()
+@click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration())
+def run(timeout):
+    click.echo(timeout)
+```
+
